Sam U. Rai-Sam-Hum-Mal-Law died in the Dungeons of Doom on level 4
(max 6). Killed by a giant ant, while helpless.

An originally human male samurai, things went fairly normal until
about level three, when I fat-fingered and killed my dog by mistake.
Same level, saw a floating eye. E-worded, again fat-fingering to use
my katana instead of the orcish dagger I had, dulling it to -3. That
done, I throw my katana, the dagger, and an iron ring at the floating
eye. Dead. No corpse. Move on. At level 4, a kitten spawned, and I
killed and (WHOOPS!) ate it. The monster spawn count went way up, with
a P.O.ed God, I continued on, watching the turn count. (Hint to
extinctionists: Eat Cats and Dogs.) I went down to level 6, found the
oracle level, but apparently no door. (I searched every wall
repeatedly.) So, I went back up to look for the secret door elsewhere.
Eventually, I got back up to level 4. Still the same massive spawn
rate. A leprechaun spawned, and stole my gold (wasn't paying
attention), so off I go after it. Find, it flees, and I'm ...cornered
in a dead-end hallway by a werejackal. Fight it, it changes. E-word.
It flees, I chase. Throw my katana again. Hit. Get reckless and melee
it. Bitten, and infected. Kill it. Pray. Still angry god docks me a
level. Kill a lichen, back up. Corpse still there, hungry. (It'd been
about 7 turns.) Again, whoops, eat it. AngriER god. Changed. #monster.
Getting hungry. Soldier ants. Faining. Sudden realization I haven't
had anything to eat since blasphemy since the FIRST time I was on
level 4. Pray again. Another level dock. Return to human just in time
to pass out and be eaten alive by ants.

YASD x10,000, but it sure as heck was fun!


